enchilada: no IOKit-daemon busy hold at mss>=9, so IOKit quiesces for configd and wifid (after topaz 0128)

StartIOKitMatching() takes a busy count on the registry root until the IOKit daemon
(kernelmanagerd) says it has launched. It never runs on this port (no kexts; no exec in any boot
log), so the root stays busy for ever: IOKit never quiesces, configd's InterfaceNamer never names
network interfaces (no "Wi-Fi" network service) and wifid waits for it at boot (topaz 0128 saw
SpringBoard held up behind wifid). With boot-arg mss>=9 (the 0268 Wi-Fi integration) the hold is
not taken, and iokitDaemonLaunched() does not drop one it did not take. Other boots unchanged.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -1200,6 +1200,10 @@
 	}
 	IOServiceTrace(IOSERVICE_KEXTD_READY, 0, 0, 0, 0);
 	startDeferredMatches();
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+	extern bool gSweetNoIOKitDaemonHold;    /* IOStartIOKit.cpp, 0269: no hold was taken */
+	if (!gSweetNoIOKitDaemonHold)
+#endif
 	getServiceRoot()->adjustBusy(-1);
 	IOService::publishUserResource(gIOResourceIOKitKey);
 #endif /* !NO_KEXTD */
